{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556949-fetch-pilgrims-in-the-modern-era","id":1556949,"title":"Fetch Pilgrims in the modern era","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-23T23:00:17-08:00","id":1556949,"title":"Fetch Pilgrims in the modern era","content":"In the Seven Wonders setting in Dark Eras 2, we're treated to the idea that fetches can use the intertwining of Pyros and Glamour in that setting to initiate Pilgrimages of their own, just like Prometheans; and it's when a fetch very neatly succeeds at achieving the New Dawn that the Gentry sit up, take notice, and start working to tear down the Seven Wonders that enabled it. <br /> <br /> This would imply that fetches undergoing the Pilgrimage is no longer possible. But that's boring; and besides, I have a modern fetch in mind that I'd like to send on a Pilgrimage. So: while it's not <i>easy </i>to do, how might (say) a freak accident or herculean effort of some sort result in a fetch gaining Azoth and Pilgrimage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T01:06:58-08:00","id":1556956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556949-fetch-pilgrims-in-the-modern-era#post1556949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Seven Wonders setting in Dark Eras 2, we're treated to the idea that fetches can use the intertwining of Pyros and Glamour in that setting to initiate Pilgrimages of their own, just like Prometheans; and it's when a fetch very neatly succeeds at achieving the New Dawn that the Gentry sit up, take notice, and start working to tear down the Seven Wonders that enabled it.<br /> <br /> This would imply that fetches undergoing the Pilgrimage is no longer possible. But that's boring; and besides, I have a modern fetch in mind that I'd like to send on a Pilgrimage. So: while it's not <i>easy </i>to do, how might (say) a freak accident or herculean effort of some sort result in a fetch gaining Azoth and Pilgrimage?</div> </div> </div> </div>It s a bit of a stretch, but you could rule that when a changeling seal a bargain with a Promethean his fetch gain the possibility.<br /> In each case i suggest that the will of the fetch to start the Pilgrimage is mandatory to start the transformation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T18:56:16-08:00","id":1556977,"title":"","content":"Azoth does weird stuff all by itself. Stranger things than Fetches can become Prometheans, sometimes spontaneously, without a creator.<br /> <br /> I'd say any Fetch exposed to large quantities of Azoth, regardless if it's a Firestorm or involves a Promethean at all, has as much of a chance at becoming a &quot;Promethean&quot; as you want. It may also happen upon the Fetch's creation, regardless of whatever the Gentry wants or knows about it. Especially if the resulting storm fits enough to the climax of the scene that the story-driven Fae can't help but think it was just the scene's natural progression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T23:53:09-08:00","id":1556978,"title":"","content":"I could work with that. I don't think the storyline works with her having been a pseudo-Promethean from the start (I'm using reversed time shenanigans where the changeling's Durance lasted months, but she found that enough time had passed for her daughter to grow up in her absence; so the fetch is now old enough to be her mother); but I could see introducing a Firestorm sometime after the changeling returns. <br /> <br /> The one catch is that that kind of implies that the fetch is actually an Extempore; and I'm still debating if I actually want her to have Azoth, a Bestowment, and Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T17:07:27-08:00","id":1557014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1556949-fetch-pilgrims-in-the-modern-era?p=1556978#post1556978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one catch is that that kind of implies that the fetch is actually an Extempore; and I'm still debating if I actually want her to have Azoth, a Bestowment, and Transmutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, the Free-form nature of an Extempore's Bestowment means you can use them to built in her nature as a Fetch or a Hedge Denizen of sorts. And Azoth and Transmutations, while mechanically Splat features, metaphysically are a result of the Alchemical process within, not the nature of the body.<br /> <br /> That said, again, Azoth does weird stuff. Even in an actual Promethean game, a created that's mechanically another splat with Pilgrimage tackled to them isn't really out of place. So do as you will, this is the most forgiving phenomenon in the game to explain the world going bananas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-26T20:55:26-08:00","id":1557033,"title":"","content":"A few notable things from The Seven Wonders:<br /> <br /> 1. The sidebar in the court writeup for the Dream Builders suggests the creations of changeling genitors take cues from typical fetch construction techniques and are mechanically Extempore who no longer have sufficiently powerful Fire to sustain them after the end of the Miasma, this being distinct from the mechanics provided for playing as fetches, which seem to mainly just give them the ability to purchase Goblin Contracts.<br /> <br /> 2. While it isn't outright stated that this is what the Great Bargain is, there's enough bits floating around the chapter to make it clear that this is a Dark Era built around a bit of Contagion-adjacent phenomenon.<br /> <br /> 3. The Colossus of Rhodes is implied through story hooks to be the &quot;Hedgebound construct&quot; alluded to in the opening crawl of the chapter, and thus the ability of fetches to start a Pilgrimage is contingent upon the existence of a Promethean (an Extempore who has budded off a Lineage of its own) who is an engineered weak point in the Great Bargain that maintains the Miasma.<br /> <br /> That out of the way, barring the perennial option of leaning into &quot;the world just works differently than usual in this game&quot; or relying on million-to-one unique and unexplained phenomena, the parallel scenario is that some arrangement of magical phenomena, whether by happenstance or deliberate construction, is allowing this to happen as an individual, regional, global, or universal phenomenon during a particular point in time.<br /> <br /> This could be accomplished a number of ways, from directly mirroring the Seven Wonders through an unexpected interaction between a big piece of pledgecraft and the Divine Fire to an elaborate scheme that the fetch is a convenient or essential component of to incorporating an Athanor or Azothic Object.<br /> <br /> As with, say, devising Infrastructure, it's important to figure out (at least to the point of knowing if you want it to be deliberately ambiguous) the technical bounds of the phenomenon allowing a fetch to start on the Pilgrimage. Is the effect permanent once joined, or does it rely on sustaining the configuration that allowed it to work? Are its effects limited geographically, temporally, and/or personally? What caused this, was it deliberate on someone or something's part, who knows about it, and is anyone working to exploit or end it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}